&lt;h2&gt;About Capco&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Capco is a global technology and business consultancy focused on the financial services and energy sectors. We bring together industry expertise, technology and innovative thinking to help our clients navigate complex transformations and create lasting impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In Belgium, our consultants work closely with leading financial institutions on strategic business and technology transformation initiatives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an experienced &lt;strong&gt;Scrum Master&lt;/strong&gt; to join Capco’s consulting team and support one of our clients within the financial services industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will join a multidisciplinary team,&amp;nbsp;where the focus is on creating, maintaining and continuously improving &lt;strong&gt;automation solutions, including robots and chatbots&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team works with technologies such as &lt;strong&gt;Blue Prism&lt;/strong&gt; to automate processes and improve the way client services are delivered.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Scrum Master, your role is to enable the team to perform at its best. You will facilitate the Agile way of working, help remove impediments, strengthen collaboration and support continuous improvement across the team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with the Product Owner, technology specialists, business stakeholders and other teams to ensure smooth and effective delivery.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Facilitate Agile ceremonies including Sprint Planning, Daily Scrums, Sprint Reviews, Retrospectives and backlog refinement sessions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CAPCO POLAND&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;*We are looking for Poland based candidate.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Capco Poland,&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;we’re not just another consultancy - we’re the spark behind digital transformation in the financial world. As a global leader in technology and management consulting, we thrive on helping clients tackle the toughest challenges across banking, payments, capital markets, wealth, and asset management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;DevSecOps Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to provide support for our client in the insurance sector, helping embed security into cloud infrastructure and delivery processes. You will work across AWS and Azure, combining Infrastructure as Code, automation, CI/CD security, and developer enablement to build secure-by-default, scalable cloud environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Policy-as-Code &amp;amp; Guardrails: Write, test, and deploy automated policy guardrails using Infrastructure as Code (IaC) linting and scanning tools (e.g., Checkov, Tfsec, OPA/Rego) to catch misconfigurations before they reach production.&lt;/li&gt;
